<title>ITALY: Italian bonds/futures closing report.</title>
<headline>Italian bonds/futures closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian bonds and futures closed un on Friday but were soggy and not far off session lows in a quiet, directionless market looking to the U.S. for fresh news and impetus, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The March Btp Liffe future traded sideways for most of the day between 131.55 and 131.70,&quot; one dealer said, noting U.S. Treasuries stayed depressed in a thin market after weaker than expected December home sales. The focus was now on the fourth quarter Employment Cost Index due out at 1330 GMT on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The March Btp ended 13 basis points up at 131.58 after an early 131.90 high and 131.53 low.</p>
</text>
